"Python is a dynamically typed language, meaning variable declaration is not required. However, 
it supports optional static typing via Type Hints to improve code readability and tooling support."
eg Name = "Eswar"
name: str = "Eswar"

📦 Python Variables
│
├── 🔢 Numbers
│   ├── Integers (Whole numbers like 5, 100) eg : Total_Interfaces = 5
│   └── Floats (Decimals like 3.14, 2.5)  eg : System_Uptime = 3.14
│
├── 📝 Text
│   └── Strings (Words inside quotes like "Eswar")  Name_Of_Person = "Eswar"
│
├── 💡 Logic
│   └── Booleans (True or False)   Is_Interface_Up = True
│
└── 🎒 Collections (Grouping things together) 
    ├── Lists (Ordered groups: [1, 2, 3]) Ip_List = ["10.1.1.1","10.1.1.2","10.1.1.3"]
    ├── Dictionaries (Key-Value pairs: {"name": "Sam"}) Router_Interfaces = { "G1/0": "eth1" , "G1/0/1": "eth2"}
    └── Tuples (Fixed groups: (1, 2, 3)) devices = (1,2,3)
